WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:03.800
Crime pays... at least, it does if you happen
to be the Clown Prince.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:07.940
A recent breakdown by Variety revealed what
the stars of the year's biggest movies were

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:08.980
paid for their roles.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.800
While Joaquin Phoenix's salary for Joker wasn't
quite in line with your average lead in a

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.360
comic book film, it was nothing to laugh at,
either.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.800
Existing apart from the established continuity
of the DC Movie Universe, Joker shocked the

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.990
world by virtue of generating major awards
buzz, making roughly all of the money, and

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:27.720
being an excellent, complex film which is
open to wildly varying interpretations by

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:28.300
design.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:33.260
As comic book movies go, the flick was made
on a modest budget; it cost $62.5 million

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:38.000
dollars to produce, and studio Warner Brothers
went with an understated advertising campaign,

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.480
particularly as contrasted with your average
Marvel Studios blockbuster.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:42.760
"Avengers!

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:49.240
...Assemble."

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.360
As a result, Joker became one of the most
ridiculously profitable movies of all time,

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:58.230
surpassing $1 billion at the worldwide box
office and making Warners' brass look like

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:00.340
a bunch of geniuses for greenlighting the
film.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:03.960
One of the ways in which the flick's budget
was kept in check, though, was by paying Phoenix

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.660
a comparative fraction of what he might have
made if he'd opted for a more typical entry

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:09.180
into the comic book movie genre.

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:13.780
For his role as failed comedian turned agent
of malevolence in October's smash hit film,

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:18.610
Phoenix earned $4.5 million certainly not
a pittance, but not exactly Robert Downey,

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:19.340
Jr. money, either.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:23.970
Speaking of Iron Man, there exists the distinct
possibility that both he and Phoenix will

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:28.190
be up for statues come awards time; it sure
would be interesting to see how Academy voters

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:32.250
think Downey's role in the biggest movie of
all time stacks up against Phoenix's performance

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:35.020
in writer/director Todd Phillips' humble little
comic book movie.

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:38.020
"People… are starting… to notice."

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:43.460
Believe it or not, when it comes to 2019 franchise
films, Phoenix's salary for Joker is not only

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:46.700
on the low end, according to Variety, it's
kind of near the lowest.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:51.340
Only Jessica Chastain, who anchored September's
It: Chapter Two as the adult Beverly Marsh,

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:55.780
was paid less; she took home $2.5 million
for appearing in the Stephen King sequel,

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:00.120
and it's fair to say that this was to be expected
considering that movie's huge ensemble cast.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:04.540
As for the high end, Variety notes that Downey
will rake in a whopping $20 million for the

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:08.410
forthcoming The Voyage of Doctor Doolittle,
the same amount that he received up front

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:09.880
for his role in Avengers: Endgame.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.880
Note the qualifier "up front"; when the dust
settled on that film's record-shattering box

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:18.370
office run, Downey's back end pay had put
his total Endgame earnings at an eye-watering

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:19.560
$75 million.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:24.599
By way of comparison, Downey's co-star Chris
Evans only scored a $15 million payday for

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:26.640
his final appearance as Captain America.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:30.909
Dwayne Johnson is also in the $20 million
club, having earned that amount for his appearance

00:02:30.909 --> 00:02:33.480
in this summer's Fast and Furious Presents:
Hobbs &amp; Shaw.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:38.460
His co-star Jason Statham was paid $13 million,
while Idris Elba who portrayed the flick's

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.940
villain Brixton took home $8 million.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.219
Also noteworthy is the fact that in 2020,
the female stars of the most highly-anticipated

00:02:45.219 --> 00:02:48.879
comic book and franchise fare will be earning
paychecks much more in line with those of

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.820
their male counterparts than in years past.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:56.400
For example, after clocking a mere $300,000
to star in 2017's Wonder Woman, Gal Gadot

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:01.099
will earn $10 million to reprise her role
in the upcoming Wonder Woman 1984, an amount

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:04.740
much closer to what is typically paid out
to male stars of solo superhero films.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:09.600
Meanwhile, Margot Robbie is reportedly earning
between $9 and $10 million for returning to

00:03:09.609 --> 00:03:13.849
the role of Harley Quinn in February's Birds
of Prey, and Emily Blunt will pull down between

00:03:13.849 --> 00:03:18.600
$12 and $13 million to star in the sequel
to the hit 2018 horror flick A Quiet Place.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:22.420
Those whopping salaries are creeping ever
closer to those being paid out to established

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:26.620
A-listers like Tom Cruise and Will Smith;
the former will take home between $12 and

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:31.030
$14 million for appearing in the Top Gun sequel
Maverick, while the latter will notch a $17

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:33.500
million paycheck for starring in Bad Boys
for Life.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:37.580
Compared to those staggering totals, you could
make the argument that Phoenix was egregiously

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:41.379
underpaid for starring in Joker but you have
to keep in mind that Warner Bros. viewed the

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:44.040
film as a total gamble before it set the world
on fire.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:48.359
Somehow, we doubt Phoenix is upset; he's stated
on more than one occasion that he didn't make

00:03:48.359 --> 00:03:52.349
Joker for the money anyway, and it also seems
pretty likely that he'll have the last laugh

00:03:52.349 --> 00:03:53.400
come awards season.

